#radovan: it is important to use svn status
#         without svn ignores the svn status is useless
#         svn ignores are implemented in a very braindead way
#         (you have to edit each directory separately)
#         the easiest may be to edit ~/.subversion/config
#         but i have seen many working copies of colleagues where
#         this was not done
#         an alternative way using svn propset is this:
#         cd to the dirac root directory
#       $ for dir in `find . -type d | grep -v \.svn`; do svn propset svn:ignore -F maintenance/svn-ignores $dir; done
#         then don't forget to remove Makefile from the top-level ignores:
#       $ svn propedit svn:ignore .
#       $ svn ci -m "updated svn ignores"
